# Rank 1597 / CVE-2023-31136: postgres-nio's connection state
# machine transitioned into TLS negotiation while unread bytes
# remained in the incoming buffer, so an attacker could send
# plaintext ahead of the handshake and have it survive into the
# encrypted channel's processing (plaintext injection through a
# state transition that ignores buffered data,
# CWE-345/CWE-311; GHSA-9cfh-vx93-84vv). sslSupportedReceived in
# Sources/PostgresNIO/Connection/ConnectionStateMachine.swift took
# no buffer state: it added the SSL handler with whatever bytes the
# channel has pre-buffered. The fixing commit 2df54bc946 (the GHSA merge, "Ensure empty incoming buffer
# when TLS negotiation starts"): the method gains an
# unprocessedBytes parameter and returns
# closeConnectionAndCleanup(.receivedUnencryptedDataAfterSSLRequest)
# when it is positive, with that failure added to the unclean-shutdown
# handling set. .
#
# ATTENTION, transition-state validation. The defect is a security
# transition that ignores leftover state -- the state-machine-bypass
# family (VYQL-VAL-011 names it for device status): no rule can ask
# "does the plaintext-to-TLS transition require a drained buffer" --
# channel-state vocabulary. A binding on postgres-nio's own state
# machine would detect this library rather than the weakness.
# Measured on the real code: scanning the connection state machine
# reports zero findings at both revisions. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry.
# No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1597 records the
# transition without the buffer check and the checked form, both
# asserting reject VYQL-VAL-011: when transition-state vocabulary
# lands, the unchecked form must flip to expect.

test "rank1597: the ssl transition ignores buffered bytes"
  lang swift
  file Sources/PostgresNIO/Connection/ConnectionStateMachine.swift
  reject VYQL-VAL-011
  code
  ```
  struct ConnectionStateMachine {
      mutating func sslSupportedReceived() -> ConnectionAction {
          return .addSSLHandler
      }
  }

  enum ConnectionAction {
      case addSSLHandler
      case closeConnectionAndCleanup(PSQLError)
  }
  ```

test "rank1597: the fixed revision requires an empty buffer at the transition"
  lang swift
  file Sources/PostgresNIO/Connection/ConnectionStateMachine.swift
  reject VYQL-VAL-011
  code
  ```
  struct ConnectionStateMachine {
      mutating func sslSupportedReceived(unprocessedBytes: Int) -> ConnectionAction {
          if unprocessedBytes > 0 {
              return self.closeConnectionAndCleanup(.receivedUnencryptedDataAfterSSLRequest)
          }
          return .addSSLHandler
      }

      mutating func closeConnectionAndCleanup(_ error: PSQLError) -> ConnectionAction {
          return .closeConnectionAndCleanup(error)
      }
  }

  enum ConnectionAction {
      case addSSLHandler
      case closeConnectionAndCleanup(PSQLError)
  }
  ```
